                     <property name="bottomMargin">
                      <number>5</number>
                     </property>
                     <item>
                      <widget class="QTextBrowser" name="About_scienceBrowser">
                       <property name="html">
                        <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot; margin-top:18px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:xx-large; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Open science in Spikeling&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Spikeling makes the designs, code and scientific explanations behind its teaching tools available so that students, educators and researchers can inspect how they work, adapt them and share what they learn. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:x-large; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Inspect and adapt the tools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;The repository includes editable KiCad schematics and PCB layouts, a bill of materials, firmware and desktop software. The hardware designs use CERN-OHL-S v2, and the software and firmware carry GPL v3 licence notices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/OpenSourceNeuro/Spikeling/tree/main/Hardware&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#005393;&quot;&gt;Browse hardware designs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:x-large; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Trace the scientific methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;The Models &amp;amp; methods tab explains the equations, assumptions and limitations behind the simulated signals. Its source links identify the revision reviewed, and its references distinguish model adaptations from background reading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.2006760&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#005393;&quot;&gt;Read the original Spikeling paper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:x-large; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Make experiments easier to reproduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Recordings can be exported as CSV. To document how a recording was produced, keep the stimulus, model settings, timing and relevant software, firmware and hardware versions with it. The Software &amp;amp; device tab can copy the version information available to the app. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:x-large; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Share teaching practice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Educators can use the documentation and suggested exercises to build practicals around experimental design and neural data analysis. The project welcomes contributions such as protocols, translations, analysis notebooks and teaching materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://opensourceneuro.github.io/Spikeling/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#005393;&quot;&gt;Browse documentation and teaching resources&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/OpenSourceNeuro/Spikeling#contributing&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#005393;&quot;&gt;Contribute to Spikeling&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;These practices reflect priorities in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unesco.org/en/legal-affairs/recommendation-open-science&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#005393;&quot;&gt;UNESCO Recommendation on Open Science&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                       </property>
                       <property name="openExternalLinks">
